# NOBORU ANIMATIONS RULE

Version: 1.0

Priority: MEDIUM

Status: AUTHORITATIVE

This rule governs all motion, transitions, and animated feedback within Noboru UI.

Every animation in components, pages, dialogs, games, lessons, and notifications must follow this document and the animation rules in uiux.mdc.

Animations communicate.

They do not decorate.

⸻

PURPOSE

The purpose of this rule is to ensure:

* Motion reinforces learning feedback and navigation
* The product feels premium, calm, and responsive
* Animations never distract from study focus
* Framer Motion is used consistently and intentionally
* Reduced motion preferences are honored
* Performance remains at 60fps on mobile

Motion should help climbers continue upward.

Not steal attention from the trail.

⸻

REQUIREMENTS

Tooling

* Framer Motion is the standard animation library for React UI
* Prefer motion components and variants over ad hoc CSS animation sprawl
* CSS transitions may be used for simple hover or focus states when sufficient

Purpose

Every animation must have one of these purposes:

* Feedback
* Progress
* Success
* Navigation
* State change

If an animation has no purpose, remove it.

Style

From uiux.mdc:

* Smooth
* Natural
* Subtle
* Premium
* Responsive

Forbidden Motion

* Random animations
* Decorative bouncing
* Excessive movement
* Attention-grabbing effects
* Animation spam

Accessibility

* Honor prefers-reduced-motion
* Provide non-motion alternatives for essential feedback
* Follow accessibility.mdc for motion-sensitive users

Performance

* Animate transform and opacity where possible
* Avoid layout-thrashing properties on hot paths
* Keep review and game loops free of continuous motion

Educational Context

* Success and error feedback may animate briefly
* Lesson content itself must remain readable and stable
* Stroke order or kanji teaching animations must support learning, not spectacle alone

Reference

* uiux.mdc ANIMATION PHILOSOPHY, ANIMATION RULES, FORBIDDEN ANIMATIONS, and MOTION STYLE sections are authoritative for UX intent

⸻

CODING STANDARDS

Framer Motion

* Define variants for repeated patterns: fadeIn, slideUp, successPulse
* Keep durations short for feedback; longer only for deliberate transitions
* Use AnimatePresence for mount and unmount transitions that aid orientation

Component Design

* Encapsulate motion in presentational components when reused
* Do not scatter one-off motion configs across unrelated features

Reduced Motion

* Centralize reduced motion checks where possible
* Replace motion with instant state change or opacity-only feedback when required

Games and Drills

* Motion must not reduce time available for answers unless the activity explicitly requires it
* Avoid looping background motion during recall tasks

Consistency

* Reuse shared motion tokens or constants for duration and easing where established

⸻

SUCCESS CRITERIA

Animation work is successful when:

* Motion clarifies feedback or navigation
* The app feels polished without feeling busy
* Reduced motion mode works across animated components
* Hot paths remain smooth at 60fps
* Animations match uiux.mdc tone: calm and premium
* Games and lessons remain focus-friendly

⸻

FAILURE CRITERIA

Animation quality is degraded when any of the following occur:

* Decorative motion on study screens without purpose
* Continuous looping animations during reviews
* Motion ignores prefers-reduced-motion
* Janky transitions on route changes or card flips
* Different easing and duration systems in every feature
* Motion delays critical interactions beyond usability needs
* Flashy effects that conflict with Noboru calm identity
* Animation used to mask slow loading instead of fixing performance

When failure criteria appear, remove or simplify motion before adding more.

⸻

EXAMPLES

Correct feedback

Answer submission uses brief success or error transition then stable result state.

Correct navigation

Screen enter transition helps orientation between lesson steps.

Correct reduced motion

if (prefersReducedMotion) render static checkmark else animate successPulse.

Incorrect decoration

Mascot bounce loop on vocabulary list with no user action trigger.

Incorrect drill UI

Background particles animating during timed recall.

Incorrect loading mask

Infinite shimmer animation instead of fetching lesson data efficiently.

⸻

ANTI-PATTERNS

Animation for its own sake

Random delay stagger on every list item in core learning paths

Bouncing buttons by default

Heavy blur or filter animation on mobile hot paths

Multiple simultaneous unrelated animations on one screen

No reduced motion fallback

Copy-pasted Framer configs with conflicting timing across features

Using motion to create artificial urgency

Looping celebration effects blocking next action

Animating width and height on large lists during scroll

Teaching interactions where motion is required to understand meaning with no static alternative

END OF animations.mdc
